[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "French Defence: Advance Variation"]
[Variation "Advance Variation, Lputian Variation"]
[ECO "C02"]
[Character "positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "b4-break,space"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "5...Qb6 6.a3 Nh6"]
[Start "1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 c5 4. c3 Nc6 5. Nf3 Qb6 6. a3"]

6... Nh6 7. b4 { Black's knight on h6 guards nothing in the centre, so we strike at the c5 pawn now. } 7... cxd4 ( 7... cxb4 8. axb4 { Take with the a-pawn: we keep a pawn on b4 and the rook gets the open a-file. } ) ( 7... c4 8. a4 { Black has locked the queenside, so we support b4 and start the pawn play there. } 8... Nf5 9. g3 ) 8. cxd4 { Take back with the pawn to keep a strong centre. } 8... Nf5 9. Bb2 { The bishop finally gets a diagonal and protects d4 as well. } 9... Bd7 10. g4 { Chases the knight off f5, so Black cannot use it against d4. } 10... Nfe7 11. Nc3 { Plan: put the knight on a4 to hit the queen, keep d4 guarded and play for a kingside space advantage. } *
